From c477433c5f6a426f328e763ebe226e499ce2eecd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 12:19:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 841/913] dts: stm32: set i2c4 as secure and control PMIC on
 stm32mp157x-exx boards

On boards stm32mp157x-exx:
In order to secure i2c4, move the control of STPMIC from Linux to OP-TEE
and expose corresponding regulators through SCMI.

Also change LPTIM4 source clock to LSI, required by PSCI-OSI feature.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git b31e2411cc5bc9406077b51534fd63dbaf7dc578 dts: stm32: set i2c4 as secure and control PMIC on stm32mp157x-exx boards]
Signed-off-by: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Ia952cf5d37d83c0ea2dc3158bf611966acf0cdb0
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/593266
Reviewed-by: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
